A 'challenge' I generally play with that makes the endgame a mite more 
interesting is to boycott bags of holding.  They make carrying around
infinite amounts of stuff extremely easy.  A weapon/potion/wand for every
occasion.  Especially in the planes, it makes a big difference.  Perhaps
BoHs should get nixed, or at least toned down (cursed = 2x weight,
uncursed = 3/4x weight, blessed = 2/3x weight).

Give Vlad the Impaler something with which to impale.  Perhaps something
of the general nature of the autocursing +7 spear named Adventurerbane
(2x or 3x damage against @).  Also, more HPs, lower AC, and stoning
resistance.  I really like the concept of Vlad, but he's extremely wussy
for his depth (he's about right for a guardian of Sokoban the way he now 
is).

Level 3 magic cancellation might be slightly less airtight.  Maybe only
96% cancellation, rather than the 99.7% or whatever it now is.

Dragon scale mail completely dominates all other armor; you get a 
resistance and better AC than anything else.  Make it AC 5 or 6,
and/or limit its enchantment to +3.  Perhaps beef up the mithrils
by a point or two at the same time, make it at least conceivable to
wear something other than DSM in the endgame.

Give the demon lords an additional spell that summons 4-6 of the 
appropriate foocubi.  And make them (the lords) stoning resistant.
Make charisma/amulets of change good for something in the late game.

Give the Wizard a polymorph attack (magic cancellation might apply).
Pick 1 or 2 inventory items at random, and polymorph them as per the
spell.

Add a bigroom to Gehennom.

That's about all I can think of at the moment.  I agree, after the
castle and before the astral plane is just too easy right now.


